  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5225",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is shown to interact with P2X purinoceptors, which are ionotropic receptors that mediate cellular signaling through purine ligand binding. This interaction is supported by the presence of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a known inhibitor of P2X receptors, as a target of Mollicellin N. The shared target of this compound with HCC2218 suggests a potential mechanism of action involving P2X receptor modulation. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Mollicellin N may inhibit HCC2218 through the activation or suppression of P2X receptors, which could influence cellular processes in the tumor cell line. The consistent score across all three paths supports a robust mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
